From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: advance SM8350 diagnostic through MMIO

Generation 35 proved that the SM8350 QMP-UFS probe may acquire its clock and
regulator handles and apply the reviewed regulator loads without disrupting
USB NCM.  Advance the RAM-only discriminator through the existing DT binding
selection and MMIO resource mapping, then stop before clock-provider
registration, PHY creation, or PHY-provider registration.

The UFS host stack remains absent, so this diagnostic cannot enumerate or
access storage.

Signed-off-by: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
@@ -2223,13 +2223,6 @@ static int qmp_ufs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
-				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy")) {
-		dev_notice(dev,
-			   "ROG5 QMP-UFS diagnostic: regulator stage complete\n");
-		return 0;
-	}
-
 	/* Check for legacy binding with child node. */
 	np = of_get_next_available_child(dev->of_node, NULL);
 	if (np) {
@@ -2239,6 +2232,14 @@ static int qmp_ufs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_node_put;
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
+				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy")) {
+		dev_notice(dev,
+			   "ROG5 QMP-UFS diagnostic: MMIO parse stage complete\n");
+		of_node_put(np);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	ret = qmp_ufs_register_clocks(qmp, np);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_node_put;
-- 
2.51.0
